> "Developing a module"). The project rules are in the root `CLAUDE.md`; the steps in
> `docs/creating-a-module.md`; run `/check-module Zoo` before calling the module done.

**Purpose:** TODO: what the module manages, for whom, and what it adds to the back office, the
public site and the API.

## Resources and permissions

Permissions are `zoo-<resource>.<operation>`, generated from `Config/Module.php` (never
written by hand).

- `zoo-main` (page: `view`): the module's screen `<back office>/zoo` (`backend_path('zoo')`).
- Default grants: admin `zoo-main.*`.
- Settings: `Zoo.perPage`. Widget `zoo.main` (`Widgets/ZooWidget.php`). Scheduled
  task `Tasks/ZooTask.php`.
- Tables: `zoo_items` (one migration per table, `down()` implemented).
- `zoo-animals` (crud: list, show, add, edit, delete, all): table `zoo_animals`, `<back office>/zoo/animals`, API `api/v1/public/zoo/animals`. Generated by the code generator (definition in the Devtools wizard / `make:module --definition`).

## Main pieces

- `Config/Module.php` (manifest), `Config/Routes.php` (every back-office route has its `can:`
  filter).
- `Controllers/Home.php` + `Views/index.php` (example screen with the ES-module component
  `Assets/js/zoo.js`, `data-component="zoo/zoo"`).
- `Database/Seeds/ZooSeeder.php` (initial data), `ZooDemoSeeder.php` (demo data:
  `php spark modules:demo Zoo`).
- Texts: `Language/{ca,es,en}/Zoo.php` (same keys).

